# xcodebuild's -derivedDataPath. Deliberately NOT hidden (it was .build/ while this was a
# SwiftPM package): the build output is large, is what every consumer script reaches into,
# and hiding it made three build locations easy to lose track of. Every script and the
# README pass `-derivedDataPath build`, so products land in build/Build/Products/<config>/.
build/
.swiftpm/
# mlx-agent.xcodeproj IS committed - it is generated from project.yml by `xcodegen generate`,
# but it carries the two shared schemes (both with coverage off) and the resolved dependency
# pins (project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved), so it has to be in the
# repo. Only the per-user state inside it is ignored.
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/IDEWorkspaceChecks.plist
DerivedData/
.DS_Store
Private/
*.profraw
